As a Doppelganger Necromancer, I got the Bag of Perseus through
offering masses of corpses to Golthuube - I just camped out on level
one and sacrificed loads of items.after converting the altar here to
the chaotic way (a risk, but it paid off). Shortly afterwards three
Rothes ganged up on me when I was out of power points, and my Wand of
Draining had no charges. I was still pretty slow - I was hoping to be
crowned early on for the intrinsics to boost my game - and they killed
me before I could engrave 'Elbereth'. That's a real bummer, eh? I was
wearing a ring of slow digestion, the one item I insist on starting
with, as well as various other items. I think I'd started with a
blessed scroll of Genocide too, and genocided 'ant' to deal with Team
Ant for good. Then these Rothes came and killed me.

So anyway, you can offer for it. And I think you can get scrolls
blessed while wielding them as you sacrifice.

